  "details": "Toggles can be add in the Unity easily, which is what I'm used to, while also found hard to used to for current Accessories system. It's quite limited(looks weird to self/others/counter-intuitive) to have change avatar and have it refreshed when all you want just to takeoff(hide)one of the accessory depends on the surrounding. Like wearing sunglasses outside, take it off inside, it will become a whole micromanaging redundancy plus if the accessories limit ever being increased in the future.\n\n(* btw, the current likely workaround is add bones, bind and add anim/PB to a bone, the rest just like any props or items in the Unity)",
